      "title": "Setup and model downloads",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## LTX 2.5 Ingredients + Sol speed\n\n1. Install WeeTodd Nodes and restart ComfyUI.\n2. Accept the model licenses and place the LTX 2.5 split components under `ComfyUI/models/` or a shared root from `extra_model_paths.yaml`.\n3. Download the Ingredients IC-LoRA into `ComfyUI/models/loras/`.\n4. Select one clean composite reference sheet. Leave workflow image paths empty when sharing.\n5. Describe the sheet panels separately from the generated action.\n6. Queue the workflow only after **LTX 2.5 Preflight** succeeds.\n\nThis speed workflow uses the baked Q8 Ingredients transformer, eight real ancestral forwards, paged-speed Sol Attention, and the `speed` reference policy. The source sheet is center-cropped on a 32-pixel grid to at most about 384x224 before VAE encoding. This reduces persistent attention rows; use `balanced` or `quality` when tiny facial or accessory details matter more than speed. Sol changes the generated trajectory and is only useful when telemetry reports sparse kernel calls; small canvases may remain below its 16,000-row threshold.\n\n### Downloads\n\n- [LTX 2.5 model components](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.5)\n- [Ingredients IC-LoRA](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.3-22b-IC-LoRA-Ingredients)\n\n### Baked Q8 setup\n\nFollow the README baked-Q8 instructions to convert the transformer and Gemma pack, then bake the Ingredients adapter once:\n\n`$COMFYUI_ROOT/.venv/bin/python $COMFYUI_ROOT/custom_nodes/WeeTodd-Nodes/scripts/fuse_ltx25_paged_lora.py $COMFYUI_ROOT/models/diffusion_models/ltx-2.5-22b-distilled-transformer-q8-paged $COMFYUI_ROOT/models/loras/ltx-2.3-22b-ic-lora-ingredients-0.9.safetensors $COMFYUI_ROOT/models/diffusion_models/ltx-2.5-22b-distilled-ingredients1p2-q8-paged --strength 1.2`\n\nThe baked checkpoint is self-describing. Do not connect a separate IC-LoRA Loader or the adapter will be applied twice."
      ],
      "color": "#243447",
      "bgcolor": "#15202b"
    }
